Changes in v8:
- free_stranded also reclaims mapped leftovers with handle 0
  after successful H_FREE
- live destroy netpoll_poll_disable() (synchronize_net is not a netpoll barrier)
- poll records RX queue only when index < real_num (keep-path RPS)
- keep-path fencing moved here from the down-path patch: poll
  completion does not enable_irq, interrupt() does not schedule
  NAPI, poll_controller() and resume() do not walk queues at or
  above real_num_rx_queues
- free_tx_resources walks every TX LTB slot (IBMVETH_MAX_QUEUES),
  moved here from the down-path patch: a skip-unmap close plus a
  TX shrink while down leaked the LTBs above the new real_num
- scale-down takes the final no_buffer sample after H_FREE even
  though the lower count is already published (retire samples
  without the live-count bound); the commit message described a
  pre-publish harvest the code did not do
- mq_fallback accesses use READ_ONCE()/WRITE_ONCE()
- combined ethtool -L rolls RX back if TX does not
  reach the request
- skip unmask if set_real(keep) fails after real_num
  was lowered; still napi_enable so close/reset is
  not a second napi_disable hang. scale-down
  set_real(new_count) fail still re-enables
- skip unmap of the live set on H_FREE_LOGICAL_LAN
  fail-before-start (PHYP); do not zero handles;
  H_PARAMETER is already-free and unmaps. ndo_stop
  still returns 0. Retry H_FREE on the next open()
  before apply_mq_fallback, and on remove()
- poolN sysfs store returns -EBUSY while a skip-unmap close
  still holds the pools (after reopening a running device to
  retry H_FREE): the deferred free uses pool->size and
  pool->buff_size, which a store would otherwise change
- H_FREE_LOGICAL_LAN_QUEUE H_PARAMETER is already-free,
  same as H_FREE_LOGICAL_LAN: clear the handle and unmap
- refresh restart / schedule / cleanup comments vs
  the scale-up callers
- noted: enable_irq on prep-fail stays (PHYP: H_PARAMETER
  on enable is LISN not in range, not already-enabled)
- noted: down-path publish and max_tx floor stay later

